A SELECT list with implicit column aliases (`col alias`) fails strict SQL
statement validation but carries no SSL marker, so it still classifies as
SQL (feature.diagnostics_pipeline A22, issue #153). The lowercase `and`
must not report bare_logical_operator and `t.col` must not report
dot_property_access. The input uses the .ds.txt extension, which the CLI
classifies exactly like .ds (feature.cli_contract, feature.formatting A11).
-- input.ds.txt --
select t.batch_no batchNo, t.qty_on_hand onHand, t.lot_code lot
from stock_batch t
where t.qty_on_hand > 0 and t.lot_code is not null
-- format --
select t.batch_no batchNo, t.qty_on_hand onHand, t.lot_code lot
from stock_batch t
where t.qty_on_hand > 0 and t.lot_code is not null
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
